{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"catching-symmetric-hart","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n~416 lines of production logic live in workflow YAML run-blocks (reconcile-bridge, canary), the highest-defect shell surface (449f: 7 recommendations; the raw git commit at reconcile-bridge.yml:283). Bash here is untestable, unlintable by ruff, and bypasses the store seam.\n\n## Approach\nStrangler-fig: move workflow run-block logic into Python entry points (src/rebar/_engine or scripts/ per placement conventions) invoked by thin YAML steps; the raw git commit site routes through the canonical write seam (companion: raw-git-write lint child, which this unblocks for .github). Behavior parity reviewed step-by-step; workflow YAML retains only env plumbing and the python invocation.\n\n## Scope\n- .github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml + canary workflow: run blocks -> thin invocations\n- new Python module(s) with the migrated logic\n- tests for the migrated functions (currently untested shell)\n\n## Testing\nUnit tests per migrated function (classification, retry/backoff, alert filing paths); a workflow-level smoke via the existing bridge test patterns (tests/scripts/ bridge suite). Live parity observed over one scheduled run before closing.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Workflow run-blocks reduced to env + single-command invocations; logic lives in tested Python.\n- [ ] The reconcile-bridge raw git write is routed through the canonical seam.\n- [ ] Migrated functions have unit tests; bridge suite green.\n- [ ] One live scheduled run observed with parity (same outcomes/alerts as pre-migration).","id":"e602-1354-6778-4c0f","parent_id":"2f4c-7e5c-e782-4e97","priority":2,"tags":["shell-migration"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Shell-to-Python Tier 3: reconcile-bridge + canary workflow logic"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785640095661749001,"uuid":"635c2168-0b0d-4b77-a49f-bdba33465b44"}